H1200.definition:
from H1197 (בָּעַר);
a burning
KJV: fire.

H1201.definition:
from an unused root meaning to stink; offensiveness;
Basha, a king of Israel
KJV: Baasha.

H1202.definition:
from H6213 (עָשָׂה) and H3050 (יָהּ) with a prepositional prefix; in (the) work of Jah;
Baasejah, an Israelite
KJV: Baaseiah.

H1203.definition:
from H6251 (עַשְׁתְּרָה) (as singular of H6252 (עַשְׁתָּרוֹת)) with a prepositional prefix; with Ashtoreth;
Beeshterah, a place East of the Jordan
KJV: Beeshterah.

H1204.definition:
a primitive root;
to fear
KJV: affright, be (make) afraid, terrify, trouble.

H1206.definition:
probably the same as H948 (בּוּץ);
mud (as whitish clay)
KJV: mire.

H1207.definition:
intensive from H1206 (בֹץ);
a swamp
KJV: fen, mire(-ry place).

H1208.definition:
from H1219 (בָּצַר);
inaccessible, i.e. lofty
KJV: vintage (by confusion with H1210 (בָּצִיר)).

H1209.definition:
perhaps the same as H1153 (בְּסַי);
Betsai, the name of two Israelites
KJV: Bezai.

H1210.definition:
from H1219 (בָּצַר);
clipped, i.e. the grape crop
KJV: vintage.

H1211.definition:
from an unused root apparently meaning to peel;
an onion
KJV: onion.

H1212.definition:
probably from H6738 (צֵל) and H410 (אֵל) with a prepositional prefix; in (the) shadow (i.e. protection) of God;
Betsalel, the name of two Israelites
KJV: Bezaleel.

H1213.definition:
or בַּצְלִית; from the same as H1211 (בֶּצֶל)xlit bᵉtsel corrected to betsel; a peeling;
Batsluth or Batslith, an Israelite
KJV: Bazlith, Bazluth.

H1214.definition:
a primitive root to break off, i.e. (usually) plunder;
figuratively, to finish, or (intransitively) stop
KJV: (be) covet(-ous), cut (off), finish, fulfill, gain (greedily), get, be given to (covetousness), greedy, perform, be wounded.

H1215.definition:
from H1214 (בָּצַע);
plunder; by extension, gain (usually unjust)
KJV: covetousness, (dishonest) gain, lucre, profit.

H1216.definition:
a primitive root;
perhaps to swell up, i.e. blister
KJV: swell.

H1217.definition:
from H1216 (בָּצֵק);
dough (as swelling by fermentation)
KJV: dough, flour.

H1218.definition:
from H1216 (בָּצֵק); a swell of ground;
Botscath, a place in Palestine
KJV: Bozcath, Boskath.

H1220.definition:
from H1219 (בָּצַר);
strictly a clipping, i.e. gold (as dug out)
KJV: gold defence.

H1221.definition:
the same as H1220 (בֶּצֶר), an inaccessible spot;
Betser, a place in Palestine; also an Israelite
KJV: Bezer.

H1222.definition:
another form for H1220 (בֶּצֶר);
gold
KJV: gold.

H1223.definition:
feminine from H1219 (בָּצַר);
an enclosure, i.e. sheep fold
KJV: Bozrah.

H1224.definition:
the same as H1223 (בׇּצְרָה);
Botsrah, a place in Edom
KJV: Bozrah.

H1225.definition:
masculine intensive from H1219 (בָּצַר);
a fortress
KJV: stronghold.

H1226.definition:
feminine intensive from H1219 (בָּצַר);
restraint (of rain), i.e. drought
KJV: dearth, drought.

H1227.definition:
the same as H1228 (בַּקְבֻּק)xlit baqbûk corrected to baqbuq;
Bakbuk, one of the Nethinim
KJV: Bakbuk.

H1228.definition:
from H1238 (בָּקַק);
a bottle (from the gurgling in emptying)
KJV: bottle, cruse.

H1229.definition:
from H1228 (בַּקְבֻּק)xlit baqbûk corrected to baqbuq and H3050 (יָהּ); emptying (i.e. wasting) of Jah;
Bakbukjah, an Israelite
KJV: Bakbukiah.

H1230.definition:
reduplicated from H1239 (בָּקַר); searcher;
Bakbakkar, an Israelite
KJV: Bakbakkar.

H1231.definition:
from H1238 (בָּקַק); wasteful;
Bukki, the name of two Israelites
KJV: Bukki.

H1232.definition:
from H1238 (בָּקַק) and H3050 (יָהּ); wasting of Jah;
Bukkijah, an Israelite
KJV: Bukkiah.

H1233.definition:
from H1234 (בָּקַע);
a fissure
KJV: breach, cleft.

H1234.definition:
a primitive root;
to cleave; generally, to rend, break, rip or open
KJV: make a breach, break forth (into, out, in pieces, through, up), be ready to burst, cleave (asunder), cut out, divide, hatch, rend (asunder), rip up, tear, win.

H1235.definition:
from H1234 (בָּקַע);
a section (half) of ashekel, i.e. a beka (a weight and a coin)
KJV: bekah, half a shekel.

H1236.definition:
(Aramaic) corresponding to H1237 (בִּקְעָה)
{properly, a split, i.e. a wide level valley between mountains}
KJV: plain.

H1237.definition:
from H1234 (בָּקַע);
properly, a split, i.e. a wide level valley between mountains
KJV: plain, valley.

H1238.definition:
a primitive root;
to pour out, i.e. to empty, figuratively, to depopulate; by analogy, to spread out (as a fruitful vine)
KJV: (make) empty (out), fail, [idiom] utterly, make void.

H1239.definition:
a primitive root;
properly, to plough, or (generally) break forth, i.e. (figuratively) to inspect, admire, care for, consider
KJV: (make) inquire (-ry), (make) search, seek out.

H1240.definition:
(Aramaic) corresponding to H1239 (בָּקַר)
{properly, to plough, or (generally) break forth, i.e. (figuratively) to inspect, admire, care for, consider}
KJV: inquire, make search.

H1241.definition:
from H1239 (בָּקַר);
beef cattle or an animal of the ox family of either gender (as used for plowing); collectively, a herd
KJV: beeve, bull ([phrase] -ock), [phrase] calf, [phrase] cow, great (cattle), [phrase] heifer, herd, kine, ox.

H1242.definition:
from H1239 (בָּקַר);
properly, dawn (as the break of day); generally, morning
KJV: ([phrase]) day, early, morning, morrow.

H1243.definition:
intensive from H1239 (בָּקַר);
a looking after
KJV: seek out.

H1244.definition:
from H1239 (בָּקַר);
properly, examination, i.e. (by implication) punishment
KJV: scourged.

H1245.definition:
a primitive root;
to search out (by any method, specifically in worship or prayer); by implication, to strive after
KJV: ask, beg, beseech, desire, enquire, get, make inquisition, procure, (make) request, require, seek (for).

H1246.definition:
from H1245 (בָּקַשׁ);
a petition
KJV: request.

H1247.definition:
(Aramaic) corresponding to H1121 (בֵּן);
a son, grandson, etc.
KJV: [idiom] old, son.

H1248.definition:
borrowed (as a title) from H1247 (בַּר);
the heir (apparent to the throne)
KJV: son.

H1249.definition:
from H1305 (בָּרַר) (in its various senses);
beloved; also pure, empty
KJV: choice, clean, clear, pure.

H1250.definition:
or בַּר; from H1305 (בָּרַר) (in the sense of winnowing);
grain of any kind (even while standing in the field); by extension the open country
KJV: corn, wheat.

H1251.definition:
(Aramaic) corresponding to H1250 (בָּר);
a field
KJV: field.

H1252.definition:
from H1305 (בָּרַר);
purify
KJV: cleanness, pureness.

H1253.definition:
the same as H1252 (בֹּר);
vegetable lye (from its cleansing); used as a soap forwashing, or a flux formetals
KJV: [idiom] never so, purely.

H1254.definition:
a primitive root;
(absolutely) to create; (qualified) to cut down (a wood), select, feed (as formative processes)
KJV: choose, create (creator), cut down, dispatch, do, make (fat).

H1255.definition:
a variation of H4757 (מְרֹאדַךְ בַּלְאָדָן);
Berodak-Baladan, a Babylonian king
KJV: Berodach-baladan.Birliy.

H1256.definition:
from H1254 (בָּרָא) and H8050 (שְׁמוּאֵל); Jah has created;
Berajah, an Israelite
KJV: Beraiah.

H1257.definition:
by reduplication from H1250 (בָּר);
a fowl (as fattened on grain)
KJV: fowl.

H1260.definition:
from H1258 (בָּרַד); hail;
Bered, the name of a place south of Palestine, also of an Israelite
KJV: Bered.

H1261.definition:
from H1258 (בָּרַד);
spotted (as if with hail)
KJV: grisled.

H1263.definition:
passive participle from H1288 (בָרַךְ); blessed;
Baruk, the name of three Israelites
KJV: Baruch.

H1264.definition:
probably of foreign origin;
damask (stuff of variegated thread)
KJV: rich apparel.

H1265.definition:
of uncertain derivation;
a cypress (?) tree; hence, a lance or a musical instrument (as made of that wood)
KJV: fir (tree).

H1266.definition:
a variation of H1265 (בְּרוֹשׁ);
the cypress (or some elastic tree)
KJV: fir.

H1268.definition:
or בֵּרֹתַי; probably from H1266 (בְּרוֹת)lemma בֻּרוֹת first vowel, corrected to בְּרוֹת; cypress or cypresslike;
Berothah or Berothai, a place north of Palestine
KJV: Berothah, Berothai.

H1269.definition:
probably feminine plural from an unused root (apparently mean to pierce); holes;
Birzoth, an Israelite
KJV: Birzavith (from the marg.).

H1270.definition:
perhaps from the root of H1269 (בִּרְזוֹת);
iron (as cutting); by extension, an iron implement
KJV: (ax) head, iron.

H1271.definition:
from H1270 (בַּרְזֶל); iron-hearted;
Barzillai, the name of three Israelites
KJV: Barzillai.

H1272.definition:
a primitive root;
to bolt, i.e. figuratively, to flee suddenly
KJV: chase (away); drive away, fain, flee (away), put to flight, make haste, reach, run away, shoot.

H1273.definition:
by transposition for H978 (בַּחֲרוּמִי);
a Barchumite, or native of Bachurim
KJV: Barhumite.

H1275.definition:
probably by contraction from H882 (בְּאֵרִי);
Beri, an Israelite
KJV: Beri.

H1276.definition:
of uncertain derivation;
(only in the plural and with the article) the Berites, a place in Palestine
KJV: Berites.

H1277.definition:
from H1254 (בָּרָא) (in the sense of H1262 (בָּרָה));
fatted or plump
KJV: fat ((fleshed), -ter), fed, firm, plenteous, rank.

H1278.definition:
feminine from H1254 (בָּרָא);
a creation, i.e. a novelty
KJV: new thing.

H1279.definition:
feminine from H1262 (בָּרָה);
food
KJV: meat.

H1280.definition:
from H1272 (בָּרַח);
a bolt
KJV: bar, fugitive.

H1281.definition:
or בָּרִחַ; (shortened) from H1272 (בָּרַח);
a fugitive, i.e. the serpent (as fleeing), and the constellation by that name
KJV: crooked, noble, piercing.

H1282.definition:
the same as H1281 (בָּרִיחַ);
Bariach, an Israelite
KJV: Bariah.

H1283.definition:
apparently from the feminine of H7451 (רַע) with a prepositional prefix; in trouble;
Beriah, the name of four Israelites
KJV: Beriah.

H1284.definition:
patronymically from H1283 (בְּרִיעָה);
a Beriite (collectively) or descendants of Beriah
KJV: Beerites.

H1285.definition:
from H1262 (בָּרָה) (in the sense of cutting (like H1254 (בָּרָא)));
a compact (because made by passing between pieces of flesh)
KJV: confederacy, (con-) feder(-ate), covenant, league.

H1286.definition:
the same as H1285 (בְּרִית);
Berith, a Shechemitish deity
KJV: Berith.

H1287.definition:
feminine of H1253 (בֹּר);
vegetable alkali
KJV: sope.

H1288.definition:
a primitive root;
to kneel; by implication to bless God (as an act of adoration), and (vice-versa) man (as a benefit); also (by euphemism) to curse (God or the king, as treason)
KJV: [idiom] abundantly, [idiom] altogether, [idiom] at all, blaspheme, bless, congratulate, curse, [idiom] greatly, [idiom] indeed, kneel (down), praise, salute, [idiom] still, thank.

H1289.definition:
(Aramaic) corresponding to H1288 (בָרַךְ)
{to kneel; by implication to bless God (as an act of adoration), and (vice-versa) man (as a benefit); also (by euphemism) to curse (God or the king, as treason)}
KJV: bless, kneel.

H1290.definition:
from H1288 (בָרַךְ);
a knee
KJV: knee.

H1291.definition:
(Aramaic) corresponding to H1290 (בֶּרֶךְ)
{a knee}
KJV: knee.

H1292.definition:
from H1288 (בָרַךְ) and H410 (אֵל), God has blessed;
Barakel, the father of one of Job's friends
KJV: Barachel.

H1293.definition:
from H1288 (בָרַךְ);
benediction; by implication prosperity
KJV: blessing, liberal, pool, present.

H1294.definition:
the same as H1293 (בְּרָכָה);
Berakah, the name of an Israelite, and also of a valley in Palestine
KJV: Berachah.

H1295.definition:
from H1288 (בָרַךְ);
a reservoir (at which camels kneel as a resting-place)
KJV: (fish-) pool.

H1296.definition:
or בֶּרֶכְיָהוּ; from H1290 (בֶּרֶךְ) and H3050 (יָהּ); knee (i.e. blessing) of Jah;
Berekjah, the name of six Israelites
KJV: Berachiah, Berechiah.

H1297.definition:
(Aramaic) perhaps from H7313 (רוּם) with a prepositional prefix;
properly, highly, i.e. surely; but used adversatively, however
KJV: but, nevertheless, yet.

H1298.definition:
of uncertain derivation;
Bera, a Sodomitish king
KJV: Bera.

H1299.definition:
a primitive root;
to lighten (lightning)
KJV: cast forth.
